+  This revision optimizes the notification layer for a zero-cost MVP with no custom domain, no paid email provider, and no customer accounts.
+  <ul>
+    <li><strong>Email events leanified (§17):</strong> Reduced from 9 events to <strong>4 core emails</strong>. Skipped: payment verified as standalone, shipped, picked up, completed. The order page link is the source of truth for all status confirmations.</li>
+    <li><strong>Order confirmation timing changed (§7.2, §17):</strong> The first customer email is now sent <strong>after admin verifies payment</strong> — not at order submission. This combines "order confirmed" and "payment verified" into a single P1 email. The customer receives their order page URL on the checkout success screen and via push notification opt-in.</li>
+    <li><strong>Push notifications added (§17a):</strong> Web Push introduced as a $0 backup channel for P0/P1 events. No customer account required. Covers payment rejected, balance due, and ready for fulfilment.</li>
+    <li><strong>Resend-only provider (§24):</strong> Removed multi-provider complexity. Resend free tier is the sole email provider for MVP. No custom domain required; sender uses <code>@resend.dev</code>.</li>
+    <li><strong>Link security reinforced (§16, §27):</strong> Order access tokens are high-entropy (32+ bytes), rate-limited, and validated against phone+email cross-check for recovery.</li>
+    <li><strong>WhatsApp manual fallback acknowledged (§17a):</strong> Staff can export phone numbers and send template messages for urgent payment chasing when email/push fail.</li>
+    <li><strong>Cap management specified (§24):</strong> 100/day Resend hard limit. P0 (rejected, balance due) never deferred. P1 (order confirmed, ready) deferred to next day if cap hit. Balance-due batches &gt;80 are spread across 2 days.</li>
